{
  "description": "What an app's config.json is, for every reader that decides what the app may do (its `permissions`) or which settings it reads (`settings`): the device runtime (frameos/src/frameos/utils/strict_json.nim, read by js_runtime/app_runtime.nim), the SPA and the cloud (frontend/src/utils/sceneAccess.ts `parseAppConfig`) and the backend (backend/app/utils/app_config.py). The rule: strict JSON (RFC 8259), an object, at most `maxDepth` containers deep. A text that is not all three is no config: the device gives its app nothing, and both control planes refuse to save or publish the scene. `permissions` is the list as every reader takes it (known names, in the SPA's order; null: no list), `settings` the namespaces. A case with `nest` has no `text`: it is {\"permissions\":[\"frame\"],\"x\":[[...]]} with that many containers, the object included. Not in here, because JSON text cannot write them: bytes that are not UTF-8 (the planes never hold such a text) and an unpaired surrogate escape (the device refuses it, the planes read it: a device may refuse more than a plane, never less).",
  "maxDepth": 32,
  "permissions": [
    "shell",
    "files",
    "assets",
    "assets-write",
    "frame",
    "code",
    "store"
  ],
  "cases": [
    {
      "name": "an empty object",
      "text": "{}",
      "config": true,
      "permissions": null,
      "settings": []
    },
    {
      "name": "a plain config",
      "text": "{\n  \"name\": \"Clock\",\n  \"category\": \"render\",\n  \"settings\": [\"openAI\"],\n  \"permissions\": [\"assets\", \"assets-write\"]\n}\n",
      "config": true,
      "permissions": [
        "assets",
        "assets-write"
      ],
      "settings": [
        "openAI"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "whitespace around it",
      "text": " \t\r\n{\"permissions\": [\"frame\"]}\r\n ",
      "config": true,
      "permissions": [
        "frame"
      ],
      "settings": []
    },
    {
      "name": "every permission a JavaScript app can ask for",
      "text": "{\"permissions\": [\"files\", \"assets\", \"assets-write\", \"frame\", \"code\", \"store\"]}",
      "config": true,
      "permissions": [
        "files",
        "assets",
        "assets-write",
        "frame",
        "code",
        "store"
      ],
      "settings": []
    },
    {
      "name": "an empty list asks for nothing",
      "text": "{\"permissions\": []}",
      "config": true,
      "permissions": [],
      "settings": []
    },
    {
      "name": "no list at all",
      "text": "{\"name\": \"x\", \"settings\": []}",
      "config": true,
      "permissions": null,
      "settings": []
    },
    {
      "name": "names it does not know are skipped",
      "text": "{\"permissions\": [\"root\", \"frame \", \"Frame\", \"store\"]}",
      "config": true,
      "permissions": [
        "store"
      ],
      "settings": []
    },
    {
      "name": "what is not a string is skipped",
      "text": "{\"permissions\": [\"frame\", 1, null, true, [\"code\"], {\"x\": \"store\"}], \"settings\": [\"openAI\", \"\", 3, null, [\"github\"], \"homeAssistant\"]}",
      "config": true,
      "permissions": [
        "frame"
      ],
      "settings": [
        "openAI",
        "homeAssistant"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "a list that is not a list is no list",
      "text": "{\"permissions\": \"frame\", \"settings\": \"openAI\"}",
      "config": true,
      "permissions": null,
      "settings": []
    },
    {
      "name": "a list that is an object is no list",
      "text": "{\"permissions\": {\"0\": \"frame\"}, \"settings\": {\"0\": \"openAI\"}}",
      "config": true,
      "permissions": null,
      "settings": []
    },
    {
      "name": "another key's case is another key",
      "text": "{\"Permissions\": [\"frame\"], \"SETTINGS\": [\"openAI\"]}",
      "config": true,
      "permissions": null,
      "settings": []
    },
    {
      "name": "the last of two keys counts (it asks)",
      "text": "{\"permissions\": [], \"permissions\": [\"frame\"], \"settings\": [], \"settings\": [\"openAI\"]}",
      "config": true,
      "permissions": [
        "frame"
      ],
      "settings": [
        "openAI"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "the last of two keys counts (it does not)",
      "text": "{\"permissions\": [\"frame\"], \"permissions\": [], \"settings\": [\"openAI\"], \"settings\": []}",
      "config": true,
      "permissions": [],
      "settings": []
    },
    {
      "name": "a key written with escapes is that key",
      "text": "{\"\\u0070ermissions\": [\"co\\u0064e\"], \"s\\u0065ttings\": [\"open\\u0041I\"]}",
      "config": true,
      "permissions": [
        "code"
      ],
      "settings": [
        "openAI"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "a nested object's lists are not the app's",
      "text": "{\"x\": {\"permissions\": [\"frame\"], \"settings\": [\"openAI\"]}, \"__proto__\": {\"permissions\": [\"code\"], \"settings\": [\"github\"]}}",
      "config": true,
      "permissions": null,
      "settings": []
    },
    {
      "name": "numbers JSON has",
      "text": "{\"a\": -0, \"b\": 1E+2, \"c\": 0.5e-3, \"d\": 12345678901234567890123, \"permissions\": [\"code\"]}",
      "config": true,
      "permissions": [
        "code"
      ],
      "settings": []
    },
    {
      "name": "escapes JSON has",
      "text": "{\"a\": \"\\\"\\\\\\/\\b\\f\\n\\r\\t\\u00e9\\u0000\", \"permissions\": [\"frame\"]}",
